{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"466e98cb29b7484f1bf9242ef378b8c4bac7d9746e10d8755401b21387db9695","digest":{"component_or_area":"Jira reconciler comment-ID invariant check","key_entities":["binding_store.py","dispatch_apply_phases.py","invariants.py","reconcile.py","reconcile_helpers.py","_record_comment_id","BindingStore","BindingLifecycle.record_comment_id","bridge_state/comment_id_divergence.json","bridge_alerts","step_comment_divergence","check_comment_id_recording","_persist_and_log","_write_prev_snapshot_key_set"],"problem_keywords":["comment id recording","invariant violation","reconciler divergence","outbound comment posts","binding state mismatch","debounce alert"],"propositions":["Successful outbound Jira comment posts are counted at the _record_comment_id seam but the returned comment IDs are not always recorded locally, leaving comment_ids unchanged despite successful posts.","An alert must fire only when the same divergence (posted > 0, comment_ids gained = 0) is observed in 2 consecutive reconciler passes, not on the first occurrence.","The debounce counter and state must persist across passes in bridge_state/comment_id_divergence.json and reset when a pass successfully records comment IDs or contains no posts.","A corrupt or absent divergence state file must fail open to counter 0 without breaking the pass.","The posted-counter seam must tally every successful post even when the entry carries no local_comment_key and recording no-ops."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787481742135199001,"uuid":"2c23cde0-ff01-43c7-9d88-27edf3ac0bd1"}